      "content": "i'm not really sure what you mean by \"goblin's wit\" or \"goblin's treasure hoard\" lol. can we just stick to the technical specifics? \n\ni've already checked the moisture with a meter and it's at a stable 8% for my shop, so i don't think it's the dampness. if the chisels are sharp enough, could it be the actual angle of the bevel i'm using when paring those tips? what angle would you recommend for walnut to get a cleaner cut without the fibers lifting?",
